use ../lib/CodingRule

from ./GoCodeReviewComments import GoCodeReviewComments

export coding-rule GoCrcContexts:
    standard: @{GoCodeReviewComments}
    ruleId: contexts
    title: Pass a Context explicitly as the first parameter
    statement:
        A function that uses a context.Context should take it as its first
        parameter, usually named ctx. Default to passing a Context along the
        call chain and use context.Background only with a good reason. Do
        not store a Context in a struct, do not define custom Context types,
        and put application data in parameters or receivers before reaching
        for Context values.
    rationale:
        Contexts carry deadlines, cancellation, credentials and trace data
        across API boundaries, and they only work if every call passes them
        on. A Context hidden in a struct obscures its lifetime and which
        calls it governs.
    exceptions:
        A method whose signature must match an interface from the standard
        library or a third party library may get its Context another way.
        Because Contexts are immutable, one ctx may be shared by several
        calls with the same deadline and cancellation.
    severity: null
    noncompliant:
        ```go
        \\\
        type Fetcher struct {
            ctx    context.Context
            client *http.Client
        }

        func (f *Fetcher) Fetch(url string) (*http.Response, error) {
            req, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(f.ctx, "GET", url, nil)
            if err != nil {
                return nil, err
            }
            return f.client.Do(req)
        }
        \\\
        ```
    compliant:
        ```go
        \\\
        type Fetcher struct {
            client *http.Client
        }

        func (f *Fetcher) Fetch(ctx context.Context, url string) (*http.Response, error) {
            req, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, "GET", url, nil)
            if err != nil {
                return nil, err
            }
            return f.client.Do(req)
        }
        \\\
        ```
    languages: [go]
    tags: [context, api-design, concurrency]
    source: https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments#contexts
